Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["InfraScene", "ObjectName",
 CellID->1224892054,ExpressionUUID->"8393d601-4014-44ba-afc9-60862df940ec"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"7a6cd348-7c6c-4f87-9503-daab6fe26299"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["InfraScene"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/SyntheticInfrageometry/ref/InfraScene", 
     "WolframInstitute/SyntheticInfrageometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     StyleBox["objects", "TI"], "}"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     StyleBox["steps", "TI"], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "dafdd843-31f7-4031-af1a-1346954b124b"],
 "\[LineSeparator]",
 "is a construction: a list of object names, and a list of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraGeometricStep"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/SyntheticInfrageometry/ref/InfraGeometricStep", 
    "WolframInstitute/SyntheticInfrageometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "5374f5ad-dcc6-4e69-9ae0-f88c586e1cd7"],
 " constraints that define them.",
 "\n"
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"3672cf7e-875e-4bdc-a502-6a8d5b7d70c0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Definition: a scene names some objects and states constraints relating \
them. It is a construction written down, not yet carried out. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["FindInfraScene"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/SyntheticInfrageometry/ref/FindInfraScene", 
    "WolframInstitute/SyntheticInfrageometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "4d96bcb3-844c-46ec-baa4-7ff1dd231a04"],
 " carries it out."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"d986eb3e-9987-497e-87bc-d9db3ef4a390"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This is how a ruler-and-compass construction is expressed. Each step is a \
constraint of the form ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"object", " ", "==", " ", 
   RowBox[{"constructor", "[", "...", "]"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ea7cc6da-a490-48a2-96f7-99ba13200cac"],
 ", optionally with side conditions like ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"u", " ", "!=", " ", "v"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2bfb3d1c-00c9-4987-95fd-fbd65869bdef"],
 ". Later steps may refer to objects bound by earlier ones, so the steps read \
in the order Euclid writes them."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"10095399-b536-4c8e-9bbd-b1923440e426"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Inside a scene the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"Infra", "*"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7932ae5b-03d7-496e-aded-55c5249e6ff7"],
 " heads are ",
 StyleBox["constructors",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", not values. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"InfraPoint", "[", "v", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f5870f2e-0311-40a4-9023-83640f82ff81"],
 " names a point at ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 ". ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"InfraSegment", "[", 
   RowBox[{"p", ",", " ", "q"}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d23c0554-d94d-4f62-8cbb-5539c9cecb17"],
 " names the segment between two named points. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"InfraCircle", "[", 
   RowBox[{"c", ",", " ", "r"}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7b602ede-c92a-4915-a042-9eecac8ac609"],
 " names a circle. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"InfraIntersection", "[", 
   RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", "y"}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "62b07971-deb8-4531-bfce-a89c268a667d"],
 " names where two named objects meet. The names are ordinary symbols, so \
they must be undefined when the scene is built \[LongDash] ",
 Cell[BoxData["ClearAll"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a2d330d7-4501-47d4-88a2-dfabeed55ae5"],
 " them first."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"7b3b1ad6-5f53-4af9-9e8f-5845df9d5040"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The whole of Euclidean construction is available: circles and their \
intersections are what a compass is for, so ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraCircle"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/SyntheticInfrageometry/ref/InfraCircle", 
    "WolframInstitute/SyntheticInfrageometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "5f225566-2a75-4dee-9538-971a24b59432"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraIntersection"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/SyntheticInfrageometry/ref/InfraIntersection", 
    "WolframInstitute/SyntheticInfrageometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "17249c3e-5c8d-471d-830a-8b0879260fa5"],
 " carry most of the work. Use circles, not level sets \[LongDash] a circle \
is the geometric object, and a shell is the set it was cut from."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"b923e445-7485-4dae-995d-057f53eb803a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Accessors: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"[", "\"\<Objects\>\"", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d4674812-b7c2-43af-8090-ab6a4a022c34"],
 " the names, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"[", "\"\<Labels\>\"", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5910efec-be60-4de7-9e65-99bf14b1ffda"],
 " the step labels, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"[", "\"\<Constructions\>\"", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "bc0ab064-515f-4fbd-ba0f-23ad231aaef9"],
 " the constraint for each object, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"[", "\"\<Steps\>\"", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "46f5959a-2207-4448-b4b6-16f5dfa85e2d"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"[", "\"\<Assertions\>\"", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d70993e9-db1a-4969-8e21-96062101be0a"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"[", "\"\<DependencyGraph\>\"", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "696e99dd-98a6-4104-900e-6c57b1fefb81"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"a78c91d5-25d5-478e-913a-030563d634bb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Two practical notes. Solving is done step by step, and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"FindInfraScene", "[", 
   RowBox[{"scene", ",", " ", "g", ",", " ", "k"}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "190078b8-3fe7-402f-98bd-26ccbc2d3b11"],
 " solves the first ",
 StyleBox["k", "TI"],
 " steps, so ",
 Cell[BoxData["k"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "487f4a92-e902-494e-b2b2-a08eeb747ebc"],
 " is a step index and not a count of solutions. And each step multiplies the \
branching: a step whose object has several admissible realisations produces \
one instance per combination, so the instance count grows as the construction \
proceeds."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"0212f0cf-a86f-40ac-a1a2-71fef34541cd"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["A construction can stall.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Euclid never postulated that the two circles of I.1 actually meet, and on \
a graph they need not. The same construction that succeeds on a triangulated \
mesh has no solution on a square grid, because there the two circles share no \
vertex. That is the continuity assumption Euclid left unstated, showing up as \
an empty result."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"0546d64c-6449-4843-ad3a-a9802f4a57cc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Bind every construction to a name.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " An operand of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraIntersection"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/SyntheticInfrageometry/ref/InfraIntersection", 
    "WolframInstitute/SyntheticInfrageometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "2901a6ad-065c-4f9c-9241-0cd97a85890b"],
 " must be a name bound by an earlier step, not an inline constructor. \
Writing ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"InfraIntersection", "[", 
   RowBox[{"cA", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"InfraCircle", "[", 
     RowBox[{"b", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"4", ",", " ", "5"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "db0bd98e-aa84-47a3-96d7-283bcec5e4f0"],
 " fails, because the inline constructor is never dispatched and reaches the \
set operation with its own head intact. Give the circle its own step and \
refer to it by name, as below."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"e74f4a4b-e792-4a96-977e-d93dbc55e7c4"]
}, Open  ]],

